{
  "framework_overview": "Deciding between manual voter execution and autonomous agent delegation in Web3 governance hinges on balancing security, voter fatigue, execution latency, and financial stakes. Protocols leveraging Quack AI can implement dual-track architectures where routine, low-risk, or time-sensitive actions are delegated to AI agents, while irreversible, high-value, or existential decisions require explicit manual human signatures.",
